  "claimBoundary": "Frozen synthetic campaigns. Active probing prevented silent false settlements that no record-only rule can prevent, the practical counterpart of DR3, but only 0.3-3.5% of the baseline's, at 16-468 probes each, with correct settlements unchanged. The criterion required significance and set no minimum effect, so 'supported' carries no claim that the protection is worth its cost. The margin-critical endpoint merges the whole hidden group and is mis-specified for the trio family, where it reads 0; disclosed, not patched. Passive history was weaker and merged independents an order of magnitude more often. No real-world rates; probing assumes a touchable upstream; same control domain; no authority claim."
